Sun Aug 30 18:32:50 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.1.1+git20251009.63b22ec:
  * Raise cmake_minimum_required, dropping the package's reliance on
    the distro-wide CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM shim
  * Catch std::invalid_argument by const reference
- Upstream has not tagged since 0.1.1 (2019) and cuts no releases;
  master is that tag plus the two patches below, so track a pinned
  snapshot via obs_scm and ship patch-free
- Drop patches, both merged upstream:
  * SoapyAudio-hamlib-control-not-working.patch
  * SoapyAudio-fix-for-hamlib-4_2.patch
- Keep upstream's in-tree RtAudio 5.1.0 and declare it as
  bundled(rtaudio): rtaudio 6 dropped the RtAudioError API and moved
  device enumeration to opaque ids from getDeviceIds(), which
  SoapyAudio's index-based enumeration does not implement
- Ship the bundled RtAudio's own MIT notice as LICENSE.RtAudio.txt
- Check the module actually loads with SoapySDRUtil
- Spec cleanup: drop Group tags, switch to pkgconfig() BuildRequires
- Explicitly require soapy-sdr: the automatic soname dependency pulls
  only libSoapySDR, so the module could be installed with no SoapySDR
  client - not even SoapySDRUtil - to reach it

